   182→### Event Handling Implementation
   183→
   184→**Type-Safe Event Handling Pattern**:
   185→
   186→```typescript
   187→private handleToggle(e: Event, options: {
   188→    type?: "content" | "write" | "custom";
   189→    targetSelector?: string;
   190→    customHandler?: (element: HTMLElement, isHidden: boolean) => void;
   191→} = {}) {
   192→    const currentElement = e.currentTarget as HTMLElement;
   193→    const { type = "content", targetSelector, customHandler } = options;
   194→    
   195→    const nextElement = targetSelector 
   196→        ? currentElement.parentElement?.querySelector(targetSelector)
   197→        : currentElement.nextElementSibling;
   198→        
   199→    if (nextElement instanceof HTMLElement) {
   200→        const isHidden = nextElement.style.display === "none";
   201→        nextElement.style.display = isHidden ? "block" : "none";
   202→        
   203→        if (customHandler) {
   204→            customHandler(nextElement, isHidden);
   205→        }
   206→    }
   207→}
   208→```
   209→
   210→**Implementation Notes**:
   211→
   212→- Proper TypeScript typing for event objects and DOM elements
   213→- Flexible options pattern for different toggle behaviors
   214→- Type guards for safe DOM manipulation
   215→- Custom handler support for specialized behaviors
